### Package: `com.app.controller`

### Imports & Dependencies
- Spring MVC annotations (`@RestController`, `@RequestMapping`, `@GetMapping`, etc.)
- Security annotations (`@PreAuthorize`, `@Secured`)
- Validation (`@Valid`, `@PathVariable`, `@RequestBody`)
- Response handling (`ResponseEntity`, `HttpStatus`)
- Service injection (`UserService`)

### Endpoints Designed

| Method | Path | Description | Auth Required | Role |
|--------|------|-------------|---------------|------|
| POST | `/api/v1/users/register` | Register new user | No | - |
| POST | `/api/v1/auth/login` | Login & get JWT | No | - |
| POST | `/api/v1/auth/refresh` | Refresh access token | No | - |
| GET | `/api/v1/users/{id}` | Get user by ID | Yes | ROLE_USER, ROLE_ADMIN |
| GET | `/api/v1/users` | List all users | Yes | ROLE_ADMIN |
| PUT | `/api/v1/users/{id}` | Update user | Yes | Self or ROLE_ADMIN |
| DELETE | `/api/v1/users/{id}` | Delete user | Yes | ROLE_ADMIN |

### Key Design Decisions
1. **Versioned API** (`/api/v1/`) for future compatibility
2. **JWT Stateless auth** — no server-side sessions
3. **Role-based access** via `@PreAuthorize` expressions
4. **Proper HTTP status codes**: 201 (created), 200 (OK), 404 (not found), 409 (conflict), 400 (bad request)
5. **DTO separation** — controllers use DTOs, not entities
6. **Exception handling** via global `@ControllerAdvice`
7. **Input validation** with Bean Validation annotations

